H8600.definition:
from H6327 (פּוּץ);
a dispersal
KJV: dispersion.

H8601.definition:
from H644 (אָפָה);
cookery, i.e. (concretely) a cake
KJV: baked piece.

H8602.definition:
from an unused root meaning to smear;
plaster (as gummy) or slime; (figuratively) frivolity
KJV: foolish things, unsavoury, untempered.

H8603.definition:
from the same as H8602 (תָּפֵל); quagmire;
Tophel, a place near the Desert
KJV: Tophel.

H8604.definition:
from the same as H8602 (תָּפֵל);
frivolity
KJV: folly, foolishly.

H8605.definition:
from H6419 (פָּלַל);
intercession, supplication; by implication, a hymn
KJV: prayer.

H8607.definition:
from H6452 (פָּסַח); ford;
Tiphsach, a place in Mesopotamia
KJV: Tipsah.

H8608.definition:
a primitive root;
to drum, i.e. play (as) on the tambourine
KJV: taber, play with timbrels.

H8609.definition:
a primitive root;
to sew
KJV: (women that) sew (together).

H8610.definition:
a primitive root;
to manipulate, i.e. seize; chiefly to capture, wield, specifically, to overlay; figuratively, to use unwarrantably
KJV: catch, handle, (lay, take) hold (on, over), stop, [idiom] surely, surprise, take.

H8611.definition:
from the base of H8608 (תָּפַף);
a smiting, i.e. (figuratively) contempt
KJV: tabret.

H8612.definition:
the same as H8611 (תֹּפֶת);
Topheth, a place near Jerusalem
KJV: Tophet, Topheth.

H8613.definition:
probably a form of H8612 (תֹּפֶת);
Tophteh, a place of cremation
KJV: Tophet.

H8614.definition:
(Aramaic) perhaps from H8199 (שָׁפַט);
judicial, i.e. a lawyer
KJV: sheriff.

H8615.definition:
from H6960 (קָוָה); (compare H6961 (קָוֶה))
literally a cord (as an attachment); figuratively, expectancy
KJV: expectation(-ted), hope, live, thing that I long for.

H8616.definition:
the same as H8615 (תִּקְוָה);
Tikvah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Tikvah.

H8617.definition:
from H6965 (קוּם);
resistfulness
KJV: power to stand.

H8618.definition:
from H6965 (קוּם);
an opponent
KJV: rise up against.

H8619.definition:
from H8628 (תָּקַע) (in the musical sense);
a trumpet
KJV: trumpet.

H8620.definition:
a form of H8619 (תָּקוֹעַ);
Tekoa, a place in Palestine
KJV: Tekoa, Tekoah.

H8621.definition:
or תְּקֹעִי; patronymically from H8620 (תְּקוֹעַ);
a Tekoite or inhabitant of Tekoah
KJV: Tekoite.

H8622.definition:
or תְּקֻפָה; from H5362 (נָקַף);
a revolution, i.e. (of the sun) course, (of time) lapse
KJV: circuit, come about, end.

H8624.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8623 (תַּקִּיף)
{powerful}
KJV: mighty, strong.

H8625.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8254 (שָׁקַל);
to balance
KJV: Tekel, be weighed.

H8626.definition:
a primitive root;
to equalize, i.e. straighten (intransitive or transitive); figuratively, to compose
KJV: set in order, make straight.

H8627.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8626 (תָּקַן);
to straighten up, i.e. confirm
KJV: establish.

H8628.definition:
a primitive root;
to clatter, i.e. slap (the hands together), clang (an instrument); by analogy, to drive (a nail or tent-pin, a dart, etc.); by implication, to become bondsman by handclasping)
KJV: blow (a trumpet), cast, clap, fasten, pitch (tent), smite, sound, strike, [idiom] suretiship, thrust.

H8629.definition:
from H8628 (תָּקַע);
a blast of a trumpet
KJV: sound.

H8630.definition:
a primitive root;
to overpower
KJV: prevail (against).

H8631.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8630 (תָּקַף);
to become (causatively, make) mighty or (figuratively) obstinate
KJV: make firm, harden, be(-come) strong.

H8632.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8633 (תֹּקֶף);
power
KJV: might, strength.

H8633.definition:
from H8630 (תָּקַף);
might or (figuratively) positiveness
KJV: authority, power, strength.

H8634.definition:
probably for H8653 (תַּרְעֵלָה); a reeling;
Taralah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Taralah.

H8635.definition:
from H7235 (רָבָה);
multiplication, i.e. progeny
KJV: increase.

H8636.definition:
from H7235 (רָבָה);
multiplication, i.e. percentage or bonus in addition to principal
KJV: increase, unjust gain.

H8637.definition:
a denominative from H7270 (רָגַל);
to cause to walk
KJV: teach to go.

H8638.definition:
a denominative from H7275 (רָגַם) in the sense of throwing over;
to transfer, i.e. translate
KJV: interpret.

H8639.definition:
from H7290 (רָדַם);
a lethargy or (by implication) trance
KJV: deep sleep.

H8640.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Tirhakah, a king of Kush
KJV: Tirhakah.

H8641.definition:
or תְּרֻמָה; (Deuteronomy 12:11), from H7311 (רוּם);
a present (as offered up), especially in sacrifice or as tribute
KJV: gift, heave offering (shoulder), oblation, offered(-ing).

H8642.definition:
formed as H8641 (תְּרוּמָה);
a sacrificial offering
KJV: oblation.

H8643.definition:
from H7321 (רוּעַ);
clamor, i.e. acclamation of joy or a battle-cry; especially clangorof trumpets, as an alarum
KJV: alarm, blow(-ing) (of, the) (trumpets), joy, jubile, loud noise, rejoicing, shout(-ing), (high, joyful) sound(-ing).

H8644.definition:
from H7322 (רוּף) in the sense of its congener H7495 (רָפָא);
a remedy
KJV: medicine.

H8645.definition:
probably from H7329 (רָזָה);
a species of tree (apparently from its slenderness), perhaps the cypress
KJV: cypress.

H8646.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Terach, the father of Abraham; also a place in the Desert
KJV: Tarah, Terah.

H8647.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Tirchanah, an Israelite
KJV: Tirhanah.

H8648.definition:
(Aramaic) feminine תַּרְתֵּין; corresponding to H8147 (שְׁנַיִם);
two
KJV: second, [phrase] twelve, two.

H8649.definition:
and תַּרְמוּת; or תַּרְמִית; from H7411 (רָמָה);
fraud
KJV: deceit(-ful), privily.

H8650.definition:
probably for H766 (אֹרֶן);
a pole (as a mast or flagstaff)
KJV: beacon, mast.

H8651.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8179 (שַׁעַר);
a door; by implication, a palace
KJV: gate mouth.

H8652.definition:
(Aramaic) from H8651 (תְּרַע);
a doorkeeper
KJV: porter.

H8653.definition:
from H7477 (רָעַל);
reeling
KJV: astonishment, trembling.

H8654.definition:
patrial from an unused name meaning gate;
a Tirathite or inhabitant of an unknown Tirah
KJV: Tirathite.

H8655.definition:
plural from H7495 (רָפָא); a healer;
Teraphim (singular or plural) a family idol
KJV: idols(-atry), images, teraphim.

H8656.definition:
from H7521 (רָצָה); delightsomeness;
Tirtsah, a place in Palestine; also an Israelitess
KJV: Tirzah.

H8657.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Teresh, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV: Teresh.

H8658.definition:
probably of foreign derivation (compare H8659 (תַּרְשִׁישׁ));
a gem, perhaps the topaz
KJV: beryl.

H8659.definition:
probably the same as H8658 (תַּרְשִׁישׁ) (as the region of the stone, or the reverse);
Tarshish, a place on the Mediterranean, hence, the ephithet of a merchant vessel (as if for or from that port); also the name of a Persian and of an Israelite
KJV: Tarshish, Tharshish.

H8660.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Tirshatha, the title of a Persian deputy or governor
KJV: Tirshatha.

H8661.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Tartan, an Assyrian
KJV: Tartan.

H8662.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Tartak, a deity of the Avvites
KJV: Tartak.

H8663.definition:
from H7722 (שׁוֹא);
a crashing or loud clamor
KJV: crying, noise, shouting, stir.

H8664.definition:
patrial from an unused name meaning recourse;
a Tishbite or inhabitant of Tishbeh (in Gilead)
KJV: Tishbite.

H8665.definition:
from H7660 (שָׁבַץ);
checkered stuff (as reticulated)
KJV: broidered.

H8666.definition:
or תְּשֻׁבָה; from H7725 (שׁוּב);
a recurrence (of time or place); a reply (as returned)
KJV: answer, be expired, return.

H8667.definition:
from H7760 (שׂוּם);
a deposit, i.e. pledging
KJV: [phrase] fellowship.

H8668.definition:
or תְּשֻׁעָה; from H7768 (שָׁוַע) in the sense of H3467 (יָשַׁע);
rescue (literal or figurative, persons, national or spiritual)
KJV: deliverance, help, safety, salvation, victory.

H8669.definition:
from H7783 (שׁוּק) in the original sense of stretching out after;
a longing
KJV: desire.

H8670.definition:
from H7788 (שׁוּר) in the sense of arrival;
a gift
KJV: present.

H8671.definition:
ordinal from H8672 (תֵּשַׁע);
ninth
KJV: ninth.

H8672.definition:
or (masculine) תִּשְׁעָה; perhaps from H8159 (שָׁעָה) through the idea of a turn to the next or full number ten;
nine or (ordinal) ninth
KJV: nine ([phrase] -teen, [phrase] -teenth, -th).

H8673.definition:
multiple from H8672 (תֵּשַׁע);
ninety
KJV: ninety.

H8674.definition:
of foreign derivation;
Tattenai, a Persian
KJV: Tatnai.
